//chromium-review.googlesource.com/293922 Reviewed-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;reinauer@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="293922" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/22/293922/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4e90035731666a2b1ca4ea8f8782dc0d03bfa008" commit="3816df09cd74b3f30a14ea86102f52366297b527" commit_message="Update log estimate of binhost test phase  It turns out to take closer to 30 minutes:  https://uberchromegw.corp.google.com/i/chromeos/builders/CQ%20master/builds/10093/steps/BinhostTest/logs/stdio  So, be a bit more accurate in the printed estimate.  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I4e90035731666a2b1ca4ea8f8782dc0d03bfa008 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/325508 Commit-Ready: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="325508" owner_email="olofj@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/08/325508/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ia1a1c6ebaaa6cd82144176ffcde31842b7a78726" commit="84d815f59e7aefbcbca3a8f0b4bbd0870501144b" commit_message="Revert &quot;PM / Suspend: Print wall time at suspend entry and exit&quot;  This reverts commit 195382b8828f (&quot;PM / Suspend: Print wall time at suspend entry and exit&quot;).  Builds fail if SUSPEND is enabled and RTC_CLASS is disabled.  kernel/built-in.o: In function `rtc_time_to_tm':  include/linux/rtc.h:32: undefined reference to `rtc_time64_to_tm'  Original commit is broken, it depends on RTC_CLASS but adding an actual Kconfig depends is really heavy handed. We don't rely on these markers today so we can revert the patch for now.  BUG=chromium:583462 TEST=None  Change-Id: Ia1a1c6ebaaa6cd82144176ffcde31842b7a78726 Signed-off-by: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/325552 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="325552" owner_email="olofj@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/52/325552/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6bbe765fdf76fedf83a53c3a4226192da55356d0" commit="427f5fb3cdd01f4d2171648f61b83b58dbee501a" commit_message="CRAS: client - Close shm fd immediately  Closing the shm fd as soon as shm mmap finishes removes the chance of leaking the FD in case the user never shuts down the stream cleanly.  A crashing client was leaking file descriptors in the browser process.  BUG=chromium:582143 TEST=lsof|grep '^chrome' while adding and removing streams, don't see number of open file descriptors increasing.  Change-Id: I6bbe765fdf76fedf83a53c3a4226192da55356d0 Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/325562 Reviewed-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="325562" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/62/325562/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Ia88e1fb862003051e93e51eb6bf62e5ae81a829d" commit="35e6673f977f9ff5c190670e44c865fbd028602a" commit_message="CHROMIUM: alt-syscall: Whitelist mmap() and newfstatat() for ARM64  When adding ARM64 support I unintentionally left these two blocked.  BUG=b:26589008 TEST=Builds for Cyan and Oak.  Change-Id: Ia88e1fb862003051e93e51eb6bf62e5ae81a829d Signed-off-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/325101 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 5634c61edafb9c8266afda2819cdc4414e4a7fb6) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/325534 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="325534" owner_email="abrestic@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/34/325534/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I3b891bc2a6fbf060bdcb4efe4e33e2a821003bff" commit="f747ff02e3fcfb1ced2694ab73d38e90819d47ca" commit_message="BACKPORT: sched: Fix cpu_active_mask/cpu_online_mask race  There is a race condition in SMP bootup code, which may result in      WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 1 at kernel/workqueue.c:4418     workqueue_cpu_up_callback() or     kernel BUG at kernel/smpboot.c:135!  It can be triggered with a bit of luck in Linux guests running on busy hosts.   CPU0                        CPUn  ====                        ====   _cpu_up()    __cpu_up()         start_secondary()           set_cpu_online()      cpumask_set_cpu(cpu,          to_cpumask(cpu_online_bits));    cpu_notify(CPU_ONLINE)      &lt;do stuff, see below&gt;      cpumask_set_cpu(cpu,          to_cpumask(cpu_active_bits));  During the various CPU_ONLINE callbacks CPUn is online but not active. Several things can go wrong at that point, depending on the scheduling of tasks on CPU0.  Variant 1:    cpu_notify(CPU_ONLINE)     workqueue_cpu_up_callback()       rebind_workers()         set_cpus_allowed_ptr()    This call fails because it requires an active CPU; rebind_workers()   ends with a warning:      WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 1 at kernel/workqueue.c:4418     workqueue_cpu_up_callback()  Variant 2:    cpu_notify(CPU_ONLINE)     smpboot_thread_call()       smpboot_unpark_threads()        ..         __kthread_unpark()           __kthread_bind()           wake_up_state()            ..             select_task_rq()               select_fallback_rq()    The -&gt;wake_cpu of the unparked thread is not allowed, making a call   to select_fallback_rq() necessary. Then, select_fallback_rq() cannot   find an allowed, active CPU and promptly resets the allowed CPUs, so   that the task in question ends up on CPU0.    When those unparked tasks are eventually executed, they run   immediately into a BUG:      kernel BUG at kernel/smpboot.c:135!  Just changing the order in which the online/active bits are set (and adding some memory barriers), would solve the two issues above. However, it would change the order of operations back to the one before commit 6acbfb96976f (&quot;sched: Fix hotplug vs. set_cpus_allowed_ptr()&quot;), thus, reintroducing that particular problem.  Going further back into history, we have at least the following commits touching this topic: - commit 2baab4e90495 (&quot;sched: Fix select_fallback_rq() vs cpu_active/cpu_online&quot;) - commit 5fbd036b552f (&quot;sched: Cleanup cpu_active madness&quot;)  Together, these give us the following non-working solutions:    - secondary CPU sets active before online, because active is assumed to     be a subset of online;    - secondary CPU sets online before active, because the primary CPU     assumes that an online CPU is also active;    - secondary CPU sets online and waits for primary CPU to set active,     because it might deadlock.  Commit 875ebe940d77 (&quot;powerpc/smp: Wait until secondaries are active &amp; online&quot;) introduces an arch-specific solution to this arch-independent problem.  Now, go for a more general solution without explicit waiting and simply set active twice: once on the secondary CPU after online was set and once on the primary CPU after online was seen.  set_cpus_allowed_ptr()&quot;)  Signed-off-by: Jan H. Schnherr &lt;jschoenh@amazon.de&gt; Acked-by: Peter Zijlstra &lt;a.p.zijlstra@chello.nl&gt; Cc: &lt;stable@vger.kernel.org&gt; Cc: Anton Blanchard &lt;anton@samba.org&gt; Cc: Borislav Petkov &lt;bp@alien8.de&gt; Cc: Joerg Roedel &lt;jroedel@suse.de&gt; Cc: Linus Torvalds &lt;torvalds@linux-foundation.org&gt; Cc: Matt Wilson &lt;msw@amazon.com&gt; Cc: Michael Ellerman &lt;mpe@ellerman.id.au&gt; Cc: Peter Zijlstra &lt;peterz@infradead.org&gt; Cc: Thomas Gleixner &lt;tglx@linutronix.de&gt; Fixes: 6acbfb96976f (&quot;sched: Fix hotplug vs. set_cpus_allowed_ptr()&quot;) Link: http://lkml.kernel.org/r/1439408156-18840-1-git-send-email-jschoenh@amazon.de Signed-off-by: Ingo Molnar &lt;mingo@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit dd9d3843755da95f63dd3a376f62b3e45c011210)  BUG=chromium:583821 TEST=built  Change-Id: I3b891bc2a6fbf060bdcb4efe4e33e2a821003bff Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/325509 Commit-Ready: Aditya Kali &lt;adityakali@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Aditya Kali &lt;adityakali@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="325509" owner_email="adityakali@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/09/325509/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id2ab1072d050247417fb294c4b9a6ea926642943" commit="d3d1339527042e0b89d73e5a603542ab2df535e5" commit_message="chaps: Fix typo introduced during code refactoring  Forgot to remove &quot;== 0&quot; in two out of 3 if cases...  BUG=chromium:582629 TEST=FEATURES=test emerge-link chaps  Change-Id: Id2ab1072d050247417fb294c4b9a6ea926642943 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/325607 Commit-Ready: Alex Vakulenko &lt;avakulenko@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Alex Vakulenko &lt;avakulenko@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="325607" owner_email="avakulenko@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/07/325607/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5b02da14cf6d2eb5cc409607053dde8c1274781c" commit="4ef19bcfe33aeffb68ab307c2087e47b239627dc" commit_message="autotest: implement systemd journal collection  On systemd-enabled we use systemd-journald instead of syslog to keep log data. This change adds journal collection into autotest.  TEST=after running a test with &quot;test_that&quot; test results contain journal content BUG=b:26512883  Change-Id: I5b02da14cf6d2eb5cc409607053dde8c1274781c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/325079 Commit-Ready: Andrey Ulanov &lt;andreyu@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Ulanov &lt;andreyu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Wang &lt;wonderfly@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="325079" owner_email="andreyu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/79/325079/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I99715248d28fad32c915fde5af9faa6a4aba76bb" commit="ae51801bf476583e28a541feeb491b579957529b" commit_message="results_lib_unittests: add timeout margin to reduce flake  BUG=chromium:555643 TEST=None  Change-Id: I99715248d28fad32c915fde5af9faa6a4aba76bb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/312545 Commit-Ready: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; " f